Apply every command to a table of queues

The broker owns what spans queues: the queue table, the clock, the
message and sequence counters, and the receipt handles. A receipt handle
names its queue and arrival key rather than a queue object, so a queue
deleted and created again under the same name cannot inherit its
handles. Every queue lookup goes through one function that also expires
the queue, so no command reads a message that section 4 says is gone.

